                <pb facs="0830" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.014/89: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-05-05T14:00:00-04:00">May 5, 1943—2 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        2:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>824. For immediate attention of Under Secretary. The Associated Press carries
                    story taken from pro-Nazi Paris radio that American forces have taken possession
                    of Easter Island and <hi rendition="#italic">La Opinion</hi> and the Communist
                    paper print the despatch. The Minister of Defense<anchor n="55" xml:id="d781-f1"
                    /> has issued a denial. There is no doubt that should we want and need the
                    Island, Chilean Government would agree but Whiting’s inspection showing
                    insufficient drinking water on Island is not favorable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
